Reaffirming its primary responsibility under the Charter for the maintenance of international peace and security, and the importance of multilateralism and diplomacy in addressing international disputes,

Recalling its relevant resolutions on Jammu and Kashmir and reaffirming the principle of self-determination of peoples, and stressing the need for a peaceful settlement that respects the will of the people of Jammu and Kashmir,

Having considered the letter dated 1 July 2025 from the Permanent Representative of Pakistan to the United Nations addressed to the Secretary-General (S/2025/443),

Deeply concerned by the military escalation in South Asia in May 2025, including reports of cross-border airstrikes, exchanges of fire and other military actions, which have caused loss of civilian life, heightened tensions and threatened regional and international peace and security,

Condemning in the strongest terms the terrorist attack of 22 April 2025 in Pahalgam, Jammu and Kashmir, expressing its deepest condolences to the families of the victims, and stressing the need for a thorough, impartial and transparent investigation to bring the perpetrators, organizers, financiers and sponsors of this and other terrorist acts to justice,

